    "text": "To determine the total number of books Katy read during the summer, we need to calculate the number of books she read each month and then sum them up.\n\n1. **Books read in June:**\n   Katy read 8 books in June.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Books in June} = 8\n   \\]\n\n2. **Books read in July:**\n   Katy read twice as many books in July as she did in June.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Books in July} = 2 \\times 8 = 16\n   \\]\n\n3. **Books read in August:**\n   Katy read three fewer books in August than she did in July.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Books in August} = 16 - 3 = 13\n   \\]\n\n4. **Total books read during the summer:**\n   To find the total number of books Katy read during the summer, we sum the books read in June, July, and August.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total books} = \\text{Books in June} + \\text{Books in July} + \\text{Books in August} = 8 + 16 + 13 = 37\n   \\]\n\nThus, the total number of books Katy read during the summer is \\(\\boxed{37}\\).",
